.TH DMENU-MAC 1 "September 2026" "dmenu-mac 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
dmenu-mac \- dynamic menu for macOS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dmenu-mac
.RB [ options ]
.br
.B dmenu-mac_run
.RB [ options ]
.br
.B dmenu-mac_path
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dmenu-mac
reads newline-separated items from standard input, displays a native AppKit
menu, and writes the selected item to standard output. It exits successfully
after a selection and unsuccessfully when cancelled.
.PP
The menu floats in the center of the selected screen by default. Its width is
the greater of its natural content width and the configured minimum width,
clamped to the visible screen.
.PP
.B dmenu-mac_path
prints a sorted, deduplicated list of executables found in PATH and macOS
application bundles. Applications are emitted as full .app bundle paths and
are discovered through Spotlight plus standard application directories. It
caches the list in ~/.cache/dmenu_mac_cache and refreshes it periodically.
.PP
.B dmenu-mac_run
uses that list to select and directly execute a command.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-b, \-\-bottom
Display a full-width bar at the bottom of the screen.
.TP
.B \-t, \-\-top
Display a full-width bar at the top of the screen.
.TP
.B \-i, \-\-insensitive
Match case insensitively.
.TP
.BI \-l " lines"
Display at most this many result rows. Zero uses a horizontal result row.
.TP
.BI \-mw " width"
Set the minimum centered width in points. The default is 600.
.TP
.BI \-h " height"
Set the minimum row height in points. The default is 20.
.TP
.BI \-m " screen"
Use the screen at the given zero-based index.
.TP
.BI \-p " prompt"
Display a prompt to the left of the input field.
.TP
.BI \-po " prompt"
Display a prompt without reading standard input.
.TP
.B \-r, \-\-return-early
Return as soon as filtering leaves one match.
.TP
.BI \-fn " font"
Set the font name, optionally followed by a point size.
.TP
.BI \-bw " width"
Set the border width.
.TP
.BI \-bc " color"
Set the border color.
.TP
.BI \-nb " color"
Set the normal background color.
.TP
.BI \-nf " color"
Set the normal foreground color.
.TP
.BI \-sb " color"
Set the selected background color.
.TP
.BI \-sf " color"
Set the selected foreground color. Colors use #RRGGBB or #RRGGBBAA.
.TP
.B \-e, \-ec, \-er
Display standard input as a noninteractive left-, center-, or right-aligned
message.
.TP
.BI \-et " seconds"
Set the message timeout. The default is 3 seconds.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Control-j, Down
Select the next matching item.
.TP
.B Control-k, Up
Select the previous matching item.
.TP
.B PageUp, PageDown
Move by one visible page.
.TP
.B Tab
Copy the selected item into the input field.
.TP
.B Return
Print the selected item and exit.
.TP
.B Shift-Return
Print the input text and exit.
.TP
.B Control-Return
Print the selected item without closing the menu.
.TP
.B Escape, Control-c, Control-g
Cancel and exit unsuccessfully.
